From f9f526d0ac0e4ea940f65575fa21fa3db18e1c47 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Craig Carnell <1188869+cscd98@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 16:00:20 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] xbox: add dolby vision low latency and transform plugin

[Hades: adapted to this tree in five files whose context it has changed, at the
places where the commit puts its lines. VideoPicture already has a doviRpu of
its own in this tree (the coded RPU that the Dolby Vision bridge pairs the two
layers by, under HAVE_DVBRIDGE), so the field this commit adds to it is named
doviRpuNal, also where the Windows renderer reads it from a picture; the
buffer's own doviRpu (RendererBase.h) keeps its name. In
DVDVideoCodecFFmpeg.cpp the AV1 block of AddData() comes after the bridge's
block, just before avcodec_send_packet(), and the block of
GetPictureCommon() after the bridge's times of the picture, just before the
Dolby Vision metadata; strings.po keeps the range of ids that this tree uses
(from 39820). Nothing of it runs on Linux: WantsDolbyVisionRpu() is false
but in the Windows Store process info, and HAVE_LIBDOVI is not defined.]
